    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. looking at the environmental side of it though, do people generally see it as a viable way to actually hit climate goals, or is it just seen as a way to make money for the MTA?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some view it primarily as a strong funding mechanism for the transit authority, a significant part of the pro-side strongly believes it is a direct climate tool. The premise is that by disincentivizing driving in the most dense areas, it directly encourages the use of lower-emission public transport or active travel like walking and cycling. However, critics argue that without aggressive supporting policies, the revenue can become an end in itself rather than a dedicated catalyst for deep, systemic environmental change.",
      "source": "target",
