      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From an urban planning perspective, a \"fair\" version is absolutely possible, but it requires very specific policy design beyond just the toll itself. Fairness depends on substantial and guaranteed reinvestment of the generated funds into robust, high-quality, and affordable public transit alternatives for all income levels. Without strong supporting subsidies and better service, the system will inherently function as a toll that penalizes the necessary choice of driving for those without easy, affordable transit access.",
